            <p>
               NEW YEAR'S PARTY 1979
               …New Year’s Eve in Seattle saw one of the mostall around <hi rend="ul"
                     >amusing</hi> parties in years--local
               freaks packed the enemy’s practice studio
               to down Guyana punch + dance their hearts
               away to the <hi rend="ul">way out sounds</hi> of the Radio’s,
               The St. Bernard Quartet, The Girls, The Enemy,
               The Fishsticks, The Mystery Horns, not to
               mention an outstanding display of charisma by
               George “Johnny Ray” Gleason + The Boppin’ Sounds
               of Rick “Buddy Holly” Smith…Lots more bands but
               we can't remember ‘em all (Cheaters? Electric Tramps?)
               ...Tons of fun…stupid hats, champagne, noisemakers
               + <hi rend="ul">Everything</hi>! <hi rend="ul">Wow</hi>! (A nite to remember
               fo’ sho’!!)</p>

            <p>! -> <hi rend="ul">Photos L to R from top:</hi></p>

            <p>Rick Smith + Nina</p>

            <p>Mystery Horns Homer, Roland, + Edward Cardboard</p>

            <p>Mass Hysteria</p>

            <p>Fishsticks (World Premiere!)</p>

            <p>Tammy Smith</p>

            <p>The Enemy (Suzy + George)</p>

            <p>Gregor Gayden (St. Bernard Qt.)</p>

            <p>George… “If your Heartaches..!”</p>

            <p>Bob Kondraic w/Cambea</p>

            <p>More Hysteria (Yahoo! Yreka!)</p>

            <p>Damon (?) Titus</p>

            <p>Don Harper, Er. So on– –<hi rend="ul">Deeyow</hi>!!</p>

            <p>(Sorry if we forgot ya!)</p>

            <p><hi rend="ul">Photos</hi>: Randy Hall</p>
